# 4-bit Shift Register (SISO)

## Goal

Learn how to implement an 4-bit serial-in serial-out (SISO) shift register in Verilog and understand how data can be shifted through sequential logic one bit at a time.

## Concepts Learned

- shift register
- serial communication
- sequential logic
- clock
- reset
- always block
- bit shifting
- data storage

## Truth Table

| Reset | Clock        | Serial In | Register (Next State) |
|--------|--------------|-----------|-----------------------|
| 1      | Rising Edge  | X         | 00000000              |
| 0      | Rising Edge  | 0         | Shift left, insert 0  |
| 0      | Rising Edge  | 1         | Shift left, insert 1  |
| 0      | No Edge      | X         | Previous Value        |

