## Reflection

This project introduced me to serial data storage and movement using a shift register.

Unlike a standard register, which updates every bit simultaneously, a shift register moves stored data one position on every rising clock edge. This demostrated how sequential logic can manipulate data over time instead of simply storing it.

## Problems

No major problems occurred during this project.

The main challenge was understanding how every bit shifts simultaneously during a clock edge while the new serial input enters one side of the register.

